.TH HD-BOOTLOADER 7 "October 2026" "hd-bootloader" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-bootloader \- the hyprdebian EFI bootloader
.SH DESCRIPTION
The hyprdebian bootloader is a small UEFI bootloader that shows a menu of the
unified kernel images (UKIs) of the four most recent kernels, each in a
normal and a ZFS recovery profile, and boots the chosen one.
It comes in two packages, of which only one can be installed:
.TP
.B hd-bootloader-gfx
the graphical frontend: the menu on the wallpaper of
.BR hd-desktop ,
in its JetBrains Mono Nerd Font;
.TP
.B hd-bootloader-txt
the text frontend: the menu on the text console of the firmware.
.PP
.BR hd-bootloader-update (8)
builds the UKIs and writes them, the bootloader and
.I assets.efi
to an EFI system partition (ESP).
.I assets.efi
holds the settings, the menu and the DKMS MOK, which the bootloader hands to
the kernel so that it loads the DKMS-built ZFS module under Secure Boot.
A system with only the kernels of
.BR hd-kernel (7)
has no DKMS MOK: their ZFS module is signed with the key the kernel was built
with, and
.I assets.efi
then has no MOK.
.PP
.I /usr/lib/hd-bootloader/update-esps
runs
.B hd-bootloader-update
for
.I /boot/efi
and, when it exists,
.IR /boot/efi2 .
The kernel and initramfs hooks of the package run it when a kernel or an
initrd is installed or removed.
All ESPs are checked before any is written; a missing one makes the hook,
and with it the kernel package or apt, fail.
.SH INSTALLATION
The postinst stores the default settings of the package in the key
.B hd-bootloader
of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
with
.BR hd-config-update (1):
.IP \(bu 2
when there are no settings yet, the defaults of the package;
.IP \(bu 2
when the settings are those of the other frontend, as when switching from
.B hd-bootloader-gfx
to
.BR hd-bootloader-txt ,
the defaults of the package, keeping
.BR timeout ,
.B banner_text
and
.BR cmdline ;
.IP \(bu 2
otherwise, the settings are left as they are.
.PP
The postinst does not write the ESPs.
That happens with the next kernel or initrd, or by running:
.PP
.RS
/usr/lib/hd-bootloader/update-esps
.RE
.SH SETTINGS
The key
.B hd-bootloader
holds a JSON object.
All its fields are optional; a missing field gets its default.
A field of the other frontend is an error.
.PP
The fields of both frontends:
.TP
.B frontend
.B graphical
or
.BR text ,
the frontend of the installed package.
.TP
.B timeout
Seconds before the default entry boots; 5 by default.
.TP
.B banner_text
The text above the menu;
.B HyprDebian Bootloader
by default.
.TP
.B cmdline
The kernel command line of the UKIs, an object with
.B root
(the value of
.BR root= ,
.B ZFS=rpool/hyprdebian
by default),
.B quiet
and
.B splash
.RB ( true
by default), and
.BR extra ,
a list of more arguments.
The graphical frontend adds
.BI video= res_x x res_y
before those of
.BR extra ,
which can override it.
.PP
The fields of the graphical frontend:
.TP
.B wallpaper
The wallpaper, a PNG or other image;
.I /usr/share/backgrounds/hyprdebian/emerald\-1920x1080.png
by default.
A relative path is relative to
.IR /etc/hyprdebian .
.TP
.BR res_x ", " res_y
The display resolution of the bootloader; 1920 by 1080 by default.
It is also passed to the kernel as
.BI video= res_x x res_y\fR,\fP
so that the boot splash of
.BR plymouth (8)
and the desktop start with the same resolution.
.TP
.B font
The fontconfig name or file of the font;
.B JetBrainsMono NFM Medium
by default.
.TP
.BR color ", " selected_color
The colour of the menu labels, and of the selected label and the border of
the menu box;
.B #0066cc
and
.B #ff6600
by default.
.TP
.B border_width
The width of the border of the menu box in pixels; 5 by default.
.TP
.B work_area_size
The width and height of the menu box in percent of the screen; 50 by
default.
The texts scale with it.
.TP
.BR x_center ", " y_center
The centre of the menu box in percent of the screen; 50 by default.
.SH CHANGING THE SETTINGS
Write the whole key with
.BR hd-config-update (1),
then update the ESPs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-config-update hd-bootloader < bootloader.json
/usr/lib/hd-bootloader/update-esps
.fi
.RE
.SH SECURE BOOT
.B hd-base
generates the Secure Boot keys of the owner in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/secboot ;
see
.BR hd-secboot (7).
When the keys are there,
.B hd-bootloader-update
signs the bootloader,
.I assets.efi
and the UKIs with the db key, using
.BR sbsign (1);
otherwise it writes them unsigned, and says so.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration, with the settings under the key
.BR hd-bootloader .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-bootloader/defaults.json
The default settings of the installed package.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hd-bootloader
The bootloader, the assets stub and the scripts.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hd-bootloader/update-esps
Updates every ESP.
.TP
.I /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz\-hd\-bootloader
.TQ
.I /etc/kernel/postrm.d/zz\-hd\-bootloader
.TQ
.I /etc/initramfs/post\-update.d/zz\-hd\-bootloader
The hooks that run
.I update-esps
when a kernel or initrd changes.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dkms/mok.pub
The DKMS MOK.
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot/db.key
.TQ
.I /etc/hyprdebian/secboot/db.crt
The Secure Boot db key and its certificate, when they are there.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-bootloader-update (8),
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-secboot (7),
.BR ukify (1)
